  "stac_version": "1.1.0",
  "description": "## Snow Melt\n\nSnow Melt shows how much water the snowpack is releasing, given here in millimetres per day. Meltwater makes its way into the ground, streams and rivers, making snowmelt a key driver of spring runoff and flooding — valuable for flood forecasting, reservoir operation and early-warning systems. This layer is a demonstration subset of Waterjade's Level-2 snow products, covering the 2022–2023 winter season over Tyrol, modelled daily at 500 m resolution with the SnowMaps processing chain and the GEOtop physical model. It builds on the snow-modelling work first developed within the Digital Twin of the Alps (DTA).",
